## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end design for high-stakes, multilingual NLP with strict latency, privacy, and governance constraints. Probes integration of retrieval-augmented detection, on-device preprocessing, drift-aware evaluation, explainability, and safe rollout strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time streaming NLP
- Retrieval-augmented detection
- On-device PII redaction
- Multilingual DistilBERT variants
- Drift detection and governance
- Explainability and audit logging

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode for pipeline steps
async function infer(text, lang) {
  const redacted = redactPII(text, lang)
  const ctx = encode(redacted, lang)
  const evidence = retriever.search(redacted, lang)
  const score = detector.score(ctx, evidence)
  return { score, evidence }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure and bound the false positive rate across languages?
- How would you implement the rollback and audit logging in production?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical on-device multilingual verification, a real-world CRM concern when summaries are generated by LLMs.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-lingual semantic similarity
- Lightweight multilingual models (ONNX/TF-Lite)
- Back-translation checks and drift heuristics
- Privacy-first, on-device inference, staged rollout

## Code Example

```javascript
function fidelity(source, summary, lang) {
  const sim = crossLingualSim(source, summary, lang);
  const back = backTranslate(summary, lang);
  const drift = compare(source, back);
  return { score: combine(sim, drift), explanation: driftReason(drift) };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to set fidelity thresholds for different languages?
- How would you evaluate bias or overfitting across languages?

## Why This Is Questioned

This question evaluates end-to-end system design with competing constraints: real-time performance, multilingual support, strict privacy requirements, and operational scalability across tenants.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time streaming NLP
- On-device privacy preservation
- Multilingual ASR (Automatic Speech Recognition)
- Differential privacy (DP) embeddings
- Edge inference
- Model drift detection
- Human-in-the-loop annotation

## Code Example

```javascript
async function processAudioChunk(chunk, tenantId) {
  const text = await asrOnDevice(chunk, tenantId);
  const redacted = await redactPII(text, tenantId);
  const signal = await applyDifferentialPrivacy(redacted, tenantId);

  if (signal.riskScore > config.threshold) {
    await routeToTriageQueue(signal, tenantId);
  }
  return signal;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
To evaluate design of a real-time, privacy-preserving NLP system handling 40 languages with strict per-tenant isolation, enforceable retention, and robust rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time streaming NLP in a multi-tenant setting
- Multilingual PII/financial data detection
- In-flight redaction and per-tenant policy routing
- Edge vs cloud processing trade-offs
- Privacy-preserving data handling and auditing
- Rollback, versioning, and test strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code sketch: detect and redact PII in a streaming row
function processRow(row, tenantPolicy){
  const entities = piiModel.detect(row.text, tenantPolicy.languages);
